            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "For cross-reference: #8007 reports the same class of defect in `cpdef enum` support (`__Pyx_EnumBase` and `__Pyx_globals` as file-scope globals). Both are reachable only with `CYTHON_USE_MODULE_STATE=1` plus `subinterpreters_compatible=own_gil`, and in both cases `__Pyx_modinit_Global_init_code` takes the module-state pointer and marks it unused before assigning process-global `PyObject*`s.\n\nThe difference is that this one is deterministic — two interpreters in sequence — because the memoryview mode constants are `cdef` module-level names whose only reference is the C global, whereas #8007 needs concurrency.",
