            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> We should probably just error out on any cdef object when compiling in module state mode to avoid getting confusing runtime errors\n\nRight - we do have an existing warning for `cdef` global variables when `subinterpreters_compatible` is set. However, `subinterpreters_compatible` isn't propagated into the Cython-defined utility code (and apart from the warning, it wouldn't really need to be).  I think we should make sure that the warning (or something similar) gets shown for these cases.\n\nI'll re-open this issue to cover that (and I'll treat your other issue as a duplicate of this one).\n\nLonger-term it is the intention that this works though. But it'll be part of a bigger change to enable for `cdef` global variables rather than being special-cased for memoryviews or enums.",
